  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#constructing-form-data-set\n\nIn addition to normalizing names and values into CRLF, it should take care of unpaired surrogates. That seems clearly better. And if you inspect the network console in [this example](https://jsbin.com/kafuwo/edit?html,console,output), you'll see that at least in Chrome, that's already being done. (That example also shows it being done for FormData.)\n\nA fix for this would be to add an additional step, after \"End:\", which is similar to the previous CRLF one. The exception for this step is only values when the type is \"file\". The action is to replace the value or name by the result of [converting to a sequence of Unicode scalar values](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#dfn-obtain-unicode).\n",
